WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.430
Ready, go!

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:05.480
Hi there! You're watching 
"Hayate No Gotoku!"

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.970
It's been three years 
since the last TV series,

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:08.950
I can't lift this.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.980
and one year since the movie.

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:09.980
I made it!

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.890
Tonight, the new TV series finally starts!

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.390
Together, we three can do it!

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.010
Ready, go!

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.320
The creators put their all

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.990
We did it!

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:19.270
Hey guys! It's been a while!

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.430
into this show,

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:23.470
so that fans of the manga, other series,

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:22.080
What're you doing, Yukiji?

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:25.100
And you call yourself a teacher?

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:26.440
and our new fans are all satisfied.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.990
You're so cruel, Katsura-chan!

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.400
Relax and please enjoy the show.

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:30.730
Ow! Ow! Sorry! Sorry!

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.790
Well then, here's night one of

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.980
Ayasaki-kun! Ayasaki-kun!

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.930
Hayate no Gotoku: "Can't Take My Eyes Off You."

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:38.870
Help me, Ayasaki-kun! They're being mean!

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.300
Coming right up!

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.010
Why, you...

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.230
Gonna die...

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.040
I'm gonna die...

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.330
At this rate, someone's 
gonna discover the body

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:35.890
of an unidentified beauty 
in the Nevada Desert.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:38.880
You too?

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.570
You're a thief, too? That's mine!

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:44.510
You dare steal that from
 me, you dumb cactus?

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.920
Give it back! Give back my hankie!

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:56.550
Oh, I see. A stupid cactus 
is making me get all serious.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.550
You're certainly going to regret—

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:05.000
Hot! I burned my hand!

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:10.650
It's in my eyes! 
My eyes! Ouch!

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.660
Hayate!

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.170
He's not gonna come.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:38.820
After all, he's not my butler anymore.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:55.220
<i>It's been nine months since 
I became Miss Nagi's butler.</i>

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.590
Miss!

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.860
It's already noon!

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.330
It's time to wake up.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:09.400
Miss.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.340
It's already noon, Miss.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.920
What do you want? It's the crack of dawn...

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:21.590
No, it's already noon.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:25.720
See?

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:35.360
That doesn't turn back time.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.610
Ugh, stop bothering me, Hayate!

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.360
Can't I sleep in on my day off?

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.140
I let you sleep until noon, didn't I?

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.140
Shut up!

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.370
You idiot, Hayate! Stupid!

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.370
Hurry and get dressed, Miss.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.260
Are you trying to kill me?

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:56.670
It won't kill you to wake up at noon.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:56.670
Honestly...

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.490
Hello? This is the Sanzenin residence.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.730
Hello? This is Sanzenin...

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:13.420
No, I'm Maria and working 
as a maid. Well...

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:16.290
...the police?

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:31.500
<b><i>As the rain of crime and punishment falls</i></b>

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:36.970
<b><i>I am lonely, but won't let myself be consumed by it.</i></b>

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:41.450
<b><i>I promise to be alive tomorrow.</i></b>

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:45.400
<b><i>Even if evil leads me astray,</i></b>

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:48.440
<b><i>I will engrave in my heart the strength</i></b>

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:52.500
<b><i>To shake it all off and break through the despair,</i></b>

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.490
<b><i>As the light shines through the sky...</i></b>

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:58.520
<i>Ruka Suirenji's new album, “Gospel,” is now on sale.</i>

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:58.500
 Ruka Suirenji

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:58.500
 Gospel

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.260
<i>Live performance coming to Las Vegas!</i>

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.400
I can't believe it's 
 the end of September.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:08.470
Is there anything fun going on, Hayate?

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.660
I keep telling you, Miss...

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:16.670
If you lie like that,

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.510
I can see your underwear.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:25.170
You're a girl, so have a 
little dignity. Dignity!

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:28.180
Leave me alone.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:32.270
And if you keep telling yourself 
everything is boring,

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:35.110
you'll start to think of even 
fun things as boring.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.190
You say that, but...

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:43.870
I had such an active summer. 
Now that it's over,

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:49.200
it's like there's a big hole in my heart.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:51.710
Miss...

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:55.670
So to fill this hole in my heart,

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:57.110
I stay up late

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:59.230
playing games, reading manga,

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:01.630
and watching anime, then crash.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.790
I know all I do is play games, read manga,

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:10.220
watch anime, and crash, 
but I can't help it.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:14.220
Maybe to you, it looks like I'm 
loafing around, but really...

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.730
There's no other way it <i>could</i> look.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:22.780
I wish you'd be more active.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.460
At this rate, you won't have the energy

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:28.200
to finish your hectic second semester.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:30.440
No worries.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:33.240
I'll just stay home from school then.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:38.520
I'll take charge of my fall break...

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:42.090
<i>This isn't good.</i>

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:44.950
<i>If this continues, 
the already useless Miss Nagi</i>

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:48.040
<i>will become an even more useless loser.</i>

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.390
<i>I must try to stop this...</i>

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:54.170
I'm so bored I'm getting dizzy...

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:54.290
<i>But how...</i>

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:55.390
What's happening? What's this?

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.390
I wonder if there's 
anything good on TV.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:03.760
<i>An unidentified flying 
object was spotted...</i>

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:03.380
A shining, unidentified flying object
approaches Area 51, Nevada

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:07.460
<i>in Nevada's Area 51! 
We'll uncover the mystery!</i>

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:06.380
 Special Report
 A UFO appears!?

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:08.380
 Yaoi is on it!

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.820
<i>We asked military personnel for information.</i>

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:15.070
Did you actually see the UFO?

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.040
Yes, I did.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:20.290
There's no way a Countach 
can be found in the desert.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:23.880
It had to be a UFO.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.960
<i>Our information wasn't wrong!</i>

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:28.630
I can't believe these 
shows are still on TV...

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.730
They put so much effort into such...

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:34.920
There's a mysterious place 
called Area 51 in America...

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:35.680
Huh?

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:38.740
<i>Oh... Miss Nagi is smart enough</i>

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:41.410
<i>to skip grades and attend high school,</i>

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.190
<i>but she's argumentative 
and forgetful.</i>

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:45.740
<i>She is still only 13...</i>

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:50.400
<i>Although this UFO story is cliché...</i>

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:53.830
Footage of an alien autopsy?

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:56.540
<i>It's new to Miss Nagi.</i>

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.160
Nagi!

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:59.390
Nagi!

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:02.300
Miss Nagi, Maria-san is calling you.

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:03.760
Later!

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:06.670
I'm busy watching this 
investigative TV show!

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:09.920
Please, hurry!

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.210
I received a call from the 
Nevada Police Department.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:14.000
Huh?

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:15.810
What?

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:20.930
Your deceased father's belongings?

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:22.290
Yeah.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.170
They want me to visit America

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:26.850
and confirm whether the stuff

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:29.760
they found actually belonged to my father.

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:33.200
Can't they send it to you?

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.580
Um... They said no 'cause

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.580
the items might break if shipped,

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.870
and they aren't entirely 
sure the stuff was his.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:41.390
 <i>Ne...va...da...</i>

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:45.920
Security is tight at the 
Nevada Police Department.

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:49.580
Miss Nagi, who was your father?

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:52.790
He supposedly died in a car accident

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:55.000
near Las Vegas just before I was born.

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:59.910
 <i>Nevada
Area 51</i>

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:59.370
I've never met him,
 nor have any memory of him.

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:02.620
I don't even know what 
his last words were...

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.790
I can't believe they 
said they'd get rid

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:10.880
of his belongings if you 
don't come within 10 days.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:14.090
You do have school...

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:15.450
What are you saying?

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:19.450
There are more important 
things than school!

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:22.950
Huh?

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:28.210
I have to see if my 
father really loved me.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:31.690
<i>Area 51</i>

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:31.710
After this, how could I focus
 on school or studying?

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:33.760
<i>Sounds like...</i>

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.220
<i>...she's started making excuses.</i>

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:38.350
Although I've never known him,

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:42.930
I need to find out if 
my father loved me!

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.560
I've never cared before,

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.230
but now I have to know!

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:50.230
I must leave right away.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:52.850
Forget school! Off to America!

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:54.360
And if we have time,

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:56.740
<i>She couldn't care less about her father.</i>

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.740
let's go see aliens at Area 51!

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.850
Totally, if we have time!

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:01.490
I wonder what her father left behind.

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:04.560
Well...

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.770
Photos of a lover would
 be tragic, wouldn't it?

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:11.500
M-Maria-san...

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:16.990
<b>Connecting</b>

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:16.990
<b>Theater</b>

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:16.990
<b>Part A</b>

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:22.370
I think I'm going to start writing 
posts in 140 characters.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:25.020
Oh, yes. What a brilliant idea.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.880
But you're too late, Isumi-chan!

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:32.520
I am already posting in 140 characters!

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:36.530
What? You're already posting 
in 140 characters, Mother?

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:39.710
And my account name is GaGa!

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:40.680
GaGa?

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:44.680
<b>Connecting</b>

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:44.680
<b>Theater</b>

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:44.680
<b>Part B</b>

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:50.460
And what exactly is mother, 
AKA Miss GaGa, posting about?

00:10:51.020 --> 00:10:54.960
Mainly, just gripes about...
 raising children!

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:57.970
Gripes about raising children?

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:01.890
"So tired of my daughter's 
stupid questions." Send!

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.090
Send?

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:10.220
What do you mean, 
I can't go to America?

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:12.650
I didn't say that.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:15.090
I said I'm against you

00:11:15.090 --> 00:11:18.360
leaving now, when school starts in two days.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:20.610
Look at the calendar.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:23.870
You can go during Silver Week.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:27.290
There's no need to skip school.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:28.540
What?

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.760
It means much more if 
we go during school!

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:35.280
That's exactly what you <i>shouldn't</i> do.

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.050
What does Hayate think?

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:39.270
What about you, Hayate?

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:43.960
Don't you want to skip 
school and go to America?

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:46.580
Um... I...

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:48.520
Hayate-kun.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:52.310
Don't spoil her too much.

00:11:55.530 --> 00:12:01.070
Um... Uh... Maria-san does have a point.

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:08.950
Um, where are you going, Miss?

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:11.120
I'm leaving.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:11.580
Huh?

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.690
I can't be a hermit in a house

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:15.860
full of people who want me at school!

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:18.090
I'll be a hermit somewhere else!

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:22.100
What? What are you saying, Miss?

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:22.840
Shut up!

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:25.770
I'm going to this world's Gandhara,

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:28.500
a land where only NEETs and hermits reside.

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:31.350
That is a land where you mustn't go.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:35.150
I am leaving this house! 
Don't follow me!

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:38.610
Wa-Wait, Miss!

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:42.130
It'll be a disaster if 
you get kidnapped again!

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:45.110
Please don't come home too late.

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:45.110
Miss! Wait, Miss Nagi!

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:56.690
So you had nowhere to go but here.

00:12:57.590 --> 00:12:58.640
But...

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:03.590
Don't be selfish and
 make those two worry.

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:06.200
Wha... What?

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:09.710
You only realize the importance of

00:13:09.710 --> 00:13:11.470
something after you lose it...

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:15.010
Haven't you already learned that?

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:23.160
They'll run out of patience
 and you'll lose them.

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:27.690
You're so meddlesome...

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:32.000
It's dangerous around here lately, 
so be careful on your way home!

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:41.430
Like Chiharu understands anything...

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:42.480
 Gyokusai Park

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:44.260
I know!

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.680
Since I'm in Akiba,

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.760
I'll buy some games or 
something and head back.

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:52.320
I saw a few things I wanted.

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.140
I might as well...

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:56.520
Yikes! I ran out the door

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.380
without money or my cell phone...

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:04.400
I do have this in my pocket...

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:07.810
I wonder how much I have left?

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:14.950
Only 170 yen... I can barely get...

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:20.020
<i>Super Spicy Red Bean Drink</i>

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:18.520
No! What'd I just buy?

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:20.460
I really don't wanna drink this!

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:24.310
What to do, what to do? 
I can't even get home...

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:28.550
I guess I'd better calm 
down and drink this.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.530
<i>Super Spicy Red Bean Drink</i>

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:32.780
 <i>Super Spicy Red Bean Drink</i>

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:39.810
Oh no. It's getting dark.

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:42.360
And it's supposedly 
dangerous around here.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:48.750
There you are, Miss.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.530
Haya—

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:52.240
Wh-What is it?

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:55.520
You betrayed me earlier, you betrayer!

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:57.910
"Betrayer"? Oh, come on.

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:01.520
In any case, Maria-san is waiting.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.890
Let's go home together.

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:07.980
I won't accept help from a betrayer!

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:10.330
M-Miss!

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:14.170
If you want me to go home with you,

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:19.310
you have to drink all of my
Super Spicy Red Bean Drink!

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:23.060
What? This drink?

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:26.000
That's right. If you can drink it,

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.070
I suppose I could go home with you.

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:32.050
 <i>Super Spicy Red Bean Drink</i>

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:32.070
But why in the 
world did you buy this?

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:39.080
I just don't understand how the wealthy think,

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:41.320
Hayate Ayasaki-kun.

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:43.580
You are...?

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:46.620
An enemy? A friend?

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:49.090
A mysterious woman. 
 Otherwise known as...

00:15:49.850 --> 00:15:50.970
Princess Camelia!

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:53.090
Are you lost?

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:56.360
D-Don't you touch my head!

00:15:56.360 --> 00:15:58.620
I-It's rude!

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:02.100
I'm sorry, you're just so short that I...

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.730
Now, where did you come from?

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.860
Don't crouch down to talk to me!

00:16:08.120 --> 00:16:10.860
Don't relax your guard,
 Ayasaki Hayate!

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:15.870
You relax, but danger is upon you!

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:17.120
Just look!

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:26.020
<i>This is the part where I save the girl</i>

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:28.130
<i>and take the treasure as my reward...</i>

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:36.390
Oh!

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.890
The pitiful kidnapped princess.

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:43.270
And the knight who 
protects the princess.

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:53.400
The one who is most important to him...

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:55.610
has been stolen.

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:58.650
But what, exactly, does that mean?

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:02.120
The insolent ones have yet to realize...

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:06.380
the fatal mistake they have made.

00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:09.880
It's a one way ticket to Hell.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:13.760
No one may come into contact with it.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:15.340
Doing so...

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:18.130
incurs its wrath.

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:23.470
Oh no. Poor Miss Nagi.

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:29.320
There must be a reason 
behind the kidnapping.

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:31.260
I'm sure they're hoping to

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:34.250
exchange her for a big reward.

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:35.820
Or something.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:39.620
Like, perhaps, a treasure handed 
down throughout the Sanzenin family...

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:43.310
I'm borrowing this bicycle.

00:17:43.310 --> 00:17:45.120
What? You can't have it!

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:49.130
Besides, you have to hear me out!

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:50.130
What?

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:52.000
Then you can come with me.

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:54.520
Hey, hey! Let me go!

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:55.260
Quiet!

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:58.390
Talk and I bite your tongue.

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:16.020
It all went according to plan.

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:17.180
All right, bro!

00:18:17.180 --> 00:18:20.260
Wow! This hasn't happened for a while...

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:23.160
Huh, she's really nice and calm.

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:26.260
Well, I'm kind of used to it.

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:30.620
Anyway, you have your seat belts on?

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:32.420
What? Why?

00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:35.300
Well, um...

00:18:37.890 --> 00:18:38.800
It's dangerous.

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:46.370
Wh-What was that?

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:48.120
It's Hayate.

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:48.810
Huh?

00:18:49.050 --> 00:18:50.420
No matter what happens,

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:52.440
if I call for him, he'll save me.

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:57.530
He's my butler.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:01.730
He's Hayate Ayasaki.

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:04.020
Ugh! Shoot!

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.730
Hey, bro!

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:16.050
He's still chasing us!

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:31.260
Did we lose him?

00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:33.780
I don't see him, bro!

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:36.130
In front of you.

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:00.340
Shoot. Bro!

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:03.340
Bro!

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.470
Oh no...

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:08.970
Don't come any closer, you monster!

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:11.480
Come any closer...

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:12.780
and I'll...

00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:26.260
You really don't hold back.

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:27.870
Are you hurt,

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:30.000
Miss?

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:37.470
So who's the shorty over there?

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:45.390
Such humiliation... Humiliation...

00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:48.640
I'm sorry. Are you all right?

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:51.940
H-Hayate Ayasaki!

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:57.900
Just you remember... 
 You'll pay for this!

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:01.000
What's going on?

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:04.620
Well...

00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:06.030
Why don't we...

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:07.910
go home?

00:21:09.020 --> 00:21:09.950
Okay.

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:16.540
We're home!

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:22.050
Welcome back! Oh my!

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:24.180
She fell asleep?

00:21:24.710 --> 00:21:26.550
Um, yeah.

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:30.200
If she sleeps until morning,

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:32.560
she won't be late for school.

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:34.710
That's right.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:39.690
But anyway... Who's that?

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:40.920
What?

00:21:44.890 --> 00:21:46.200
Me?

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:48.700
I'm Ruri Tsugumi.

00:21:49.300 --> 00:21:50.950
I'm Nagi Sanzenin's...

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:53.850
little sister!

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:28.560
Katsura-chan!

00:23:27.080 --> 00:23:29.050
So! How did you like

00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:29.530
Are you dead?

00:23:29.050 --> 00:23:32.130
night one of “Hayate No Gotoku"?

00:23:29.530 --> 00:23:31.540
She's dead.

00:23:32.130 --> 00:23:36.210
The storyline will ramp up next week, so...

00:23:33.370 --> 00:23:34.980
I'm not dead!

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:37.540
Shut up!

00:23:38.420 --> 00:23:40.060
Look forward to it!
